# Alembic migrations

Alembic loads `backend/.env` and requires `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` to point to the Neon direct endpoint. Application requests use the pooled `DATABASE_URL` configured in `backend/database/engine.py`.

Run migrations from the repository root:

```powershell
python -m alembic -c backend/alembic.ini upgrade head
```

The SQLite-to-Neon data transfer is a separate one-time operation documented in the repository's `MIGRATION_CHECKLIST.md`.
